    "content": "     Domain-specific dataset enable accurate MLIPs for disordered halide-based solid electrolytes - Welcome to DTU Research Database            \n\n[Skip to main navigation](#main-navigation) [Skip to search](#main-search) [Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n[Welcome to DTU Research Database Home ![Welcome to DTU Research Database Logo](/skin/headerImage/)](/en/) \n\n-   [About DTU Orbit   Link opens in a new tab](https://www.bibliotek.dtu.dk/en/publishing/research-publishing/research-output/dtu-orbit)\n\nSearch content at Welcome to DTU Research Database \n\n-   [Home](/en/)\n-   [Profiles](/en/persons/)\n-   [Research units](/en/organisations/)\n-   [Publications](/en/publications/)\n-   [Activities](/en/activities/)\n-   [Projects](/en/projects/)\n-   [Prizes](/en/prizes/)\n-   [Press/Media](/en/clippings/)\n-   [Datasets](/en/datasets/)\n\n# Domain-specific dataset enable accurate MLIPs for disordered halide-based solid electrolytes\n\n-   Chiku Parida\\*\n-   , [Arghya Bhowmik](https://orbit.dtu.dk/en/persons/arghya-bhowmik/)\n-   , [Juan Maria García Lastra](https://orbit.dtu.dk/en/persons/juan-maria-garc%C3%ADa-lastra/)\\*\n\n\\*Corresponding author for this work\n\n-   [Atomic Scale Materials Modelling](https://orbit.dtu.dk/en/organisations/atomic-scale-materials-modelling/)\n-   [Department of Energy Conversion and Storage](https://orbit.dtu.dk/en/organisations/department-of-energy-conversion-and-storage/)\n\nResearch output: Contribution to journal › Journal article › Research › peer-review\n\n14 Downloads (Orbit)\n\n[](https://plu.mx/plum/a/?doi=10.1088/2632-2153/aea5d8)\n\n-   [Overview](/en/publications/domain-specific-dataset-enable-accurate-mlips-for-disordered-hali/)\n-   [Fingerprint](/en/publications/domain-specific-dataset-enable-accurate-mlips-for-disordered-hali/fingerprints/)\n\n## Abstract\n\nEfficient exploration of chemical space with machine-learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs) requires a comprehensive, application-focused training database. Solid-state electrolytes (SSEs) for Li-ion batteries have attracted growing attention owing to their ability to improve safety and energy density. Among these, halide-based solid electrolytes have emerged as promising candidates because of their high ionic conductivity and stability. We present an MLIP training database for Li 3 MX 6 -type halide electrolytes, where M can be group-3, group-13, and group-15 elements as well as lanthanides, and X represents halogens. The dataset covers a broad chemical space generated by varying crystallographic space groups, introducing isovalent and aliovalent doping, and including anti-site defects. It contains approximately 400k density functional theory (DFT) calculated structures with energies, forces, and stresses, together with hierarchical metadata, providing a resource to accelerate the discovery and optimization of halide electrolytes. We demonstrate the utility of the database by fine-tuning the MACE-MP-0b2-large foundation model: the energy root-mean-square error (RMSE) decreased from 154.8 to 10.0 meV atom -1 and the all-force-component RMSE from 168.3 to 39.0 meV Å-1 on a held-out test set, confirming that domain-specific training data is necessary for structurally disordered halide configurations.\n\nOriginal language\n\nEnglish\n\nArticle number\n\n050601\n\nJournal\n\n[Machine Learning: Science and Technology](#)\n\nVolume\n\n7\n\nIssue number\n\n5\n\nNumber of pages\n\n16\n\nISSN\n\n2632-2153\n\nDOIs\n\n-   [https://doi.org/10.1088/2632-2153/aea5d8](https://doi.org/10.1088/2632-2153/aea5d8)\n\nPublication status\n\nPublished - 2026\n\n## UN SDGs\n\nThis output contributes to the following UN [Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)](https://www.un.org/sustainabledevelopment/sustainable-development-goals/)\n\n1.  ![SDG 7 - Affordable and Clean Energy](/assets/sdg_icons/affordable_and_clean_energy-b8e39c169139faf6df7199566119c3c0.svg \"SDG 7 - Affordable and Clean Energy\")\n    \n    SDG 7 Affordable and Clean Energy\n    \n\n## Keywords\n\n-   Solid-state electrolyte\n-   Halide electrolyte\n-   Machine-learning interatomic potential\n-   DFT database\n-   Lithium-ion battery\n-   MACE\n\n## Access to Document\n\n-   [10.1088/2632-2153/aea5d8](https://doi.org/10.1088/2632-2153/aea5d8)Licence: [CC BY](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)\n    \n\n-   [Fulltext](/files/462981219/Parida_2026_Mach._Learn._Sci._Technol._7_050601.pdf)Final published version, 2.08 MBLicence: [CC BY](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)\n    \n\n## OpenUrl availability\n\n[Check availability in DTU Findit](http://sfx.cvt.dk/sfx_local?ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&ctx_tim=2026-10-16T23%3A37%3A02UTC&ctx_enc=info%3Aofi%2FencUTF-8&url_ver=Z39.88-2004&url_ctx_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Actx&rft.genre=article&rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Fkev%3Afmt%3Ajournal&rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fpure.atira.dk%3Apure&rft.atitle=Domain-specific%20dataset%20enable%20accurate%20MLIPs%20for%20disordered%20halide-based%20solid%20electrolytes&rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1088%2F2632-2153%2Faea5d8&rft.aulast=Parida&rft.aufirst=Chiku&rft.auinit=C&rft.date=2026&rft.volume=7&rft.issue=5&rft.issn=2632-2153&rft.jtitle=Machine%20Learning%3A%20Science%20and%20Technology)\n\n## Fingerprint\n\nDive into the research topics of 'Domain-specific dataset enable accurate MLIPs for disordered halide-based solid electrolytes'. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n\n-   Interatomic Potential Chemistry 100%\n    \n-   Halide Chemistry 100%\n    \n-   Solid Electrolyte Chemistry 100%\n    \n-   Domain-specific Datasets Keyphrases 100%\n    \n-   Focused Training Keyphrases 25%\n    \n-   Large Foundation Model Keyphrases 25%\n    \n-   Mev-1 Keyphrases 25%\n    \n-   Isovalent Doping Keyphrases 25%\n    \n\n[View full fingerprint](/en/publications/domain-specific-dataset-enable-accurate-mlips-for-disordered-hali/fingerprints/)\n\n## Cite this\n\n-   APA\n-   Author\n-   BIBTEX\n-   Harvard\n-   Standard\n-   RIS\n-   Vanc