corded quote: \"Future optimization of the workflow beyond screening will be based on the direct generation of materials with given properties, such as the method recently demonstrated by MatterGen [41].\"\n\nThis quote is not on the arxiv abstract page — it's in the body of the paper. I fetched only the abstract page of arxiv. The quote is claimed to be from the same DOI (10.48550/arxiv.2401.04070). The abstract page doesn't contain that sentence. I should fetch the HTML full text: https://arxiv.org/html/2401.04070v1 to check if the quote appears there. The DOI resolves to the arxiv abs page; but the source could be considered the paper itself. Let me fetch the HTML version to verify the quote appears in the paper.\n\n**p1:c4**: Azure Quantum Elements product leader quote: \"The vision we are working toward is generative materials where I can ask for list of new battery compounds with my desired attributes,\" Baker says. — The Microsoft news page contains: \"The vision we are working toward is generative materials where I can ask for list of new battery compounds with my desired attributes,” Baker says.\" Nathan Baker is described as \"Product Leader for Azure Quantum Elements\". Supported. The quote in the recorded text is missing the closing punctuation but matches. Status: SUPPORTED.\n\n**p1:done**: MatterGen fine-tuned on magnetic density, band gap, bulk modulus (never ionic conductivity), battery electrolyte result from screening 32M candidates rather than conductivity-conditioned generation — future-tense plan confirms generative-transport step not yet done. Source: arxiv 2401.04070. Recorded quote: the future-optimization sentence, which needs to be verified in the full text. Let me fetch the HTML.\n\n**p2:c1**: Their battery workflow uses MatterGen for structure sampling plus MatterSim/DFT screening, conditioned on convex-hull energy, not ionic conductivity. Source: doi.org/10.1002/batt.202500309 — the fetch returned only a citation stub (Parida, C., Roy, D